<title>FRANCE: EP approves market access accords with Israel.</title>
<headline>EP approves market access accords with Israel.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament approved on Friday two draft accords, COM(96)148, between the European Union and Israel on access to each others' markets.</p>
<p>The first agreement concerns government contracts, the second applies to contracts concluded by telecommunications operators.</p>
<p>The accord on public procurement complements and broadens the World Trade Organisation government procurement agreement, which entered into force on January 1, 1996.</p>
<p>According to a report by Belgian Liberal Willy de Clercq, the deals will satisfy Israel's concern for better access to EU markets for certain high tech goods.</p>
<p>They will also help open up to the EU promising Israeli markets like the urban transport sector.</p>
</text>
